      "Bash(git commit -m \"$\\(cat <<''EOF''\nfeat: Add predictive telemetry module and Docker development setup\n\nThis commit introduces Phase 7 of the mobile observability project:\npredictive telemetry with on-device intelligence for proactive issue\ndetection and mitigation.\n\n## Predictive Telemetry Module \\(Phase 7\\)\n\n### Core Components Added:\n- DeviceHealthMonitor.kt: Collects device health signals \\(memory, battery,\n  network, thermal state\\) with thread-safe caching\n- OnDevicePredictor.kt: Lightweight prediction engine using heuristics and\n  anomaly detection to predict crashes, network loss, performance\n  degradation, and battery drain \\(target <5ms latency\\)\n- PredictiveExportPolicy.kt: Pre-emptive action system that flushes buffers\n  before network loss, increases sampling before crashes, and emits\n  predictive events\n- HealthMetricsCollector.kt: Exports device health and prediction risk\n  scores as OpenTelemetry metrics\n\n### Key Features:\n- Predicts issues BEFORE they occur \\(network loss, OOM crashes, battery\n  drain, thermal throttling\\)\n- Rule-based heuristics + statistical anomaly detection\n- \"Unknown unknowns\" detection via pattern recognition\n- Integrates seamlessly with existing OTEL buffering/export system\n- Zero dependencies on cloud services \\(100% on-device\\)\n\n### Use Cases:\n- Pre-emptive buffer flush before entering subway tunnel\n- Capture crash context before OOM event\n- Reduce telemetry volume when battery critical\n- Detect novel issue patterns not in predefined signatures\n\n## Docker Development Infrastructure\n\n### Files Added:\n- k8s/docker-compose.yml: Local OTEL Collector + Jaeger UI setup\n- k8s/otel-collector-docker.yaml: Collector configuration for Docker\n- k8s/README.md: Comprehensive deployment guide covering Docker, Kubernetes,\n  network configuration, and troubleshooting\n\n### Benefits:\n- One-command setup: docker-compose up -d\n- Instant Jaeger UI visualization at localhost:16686\n- No manual collector installation required\n- Simplified onboarding for new developers\n\n## Documentation Updates\n\n### QUICKSTART.md:\n- Enhanced Step 4 with accurate docker-compose instructions\n- Added network configuration guidance \\(Android emulator vs real device\\)\n- Clarified 10.0.2.2 for emulator, actual IP for physical devices\n- Added Jaeger UI usage instructions with timing expectations\n\n### docs/OTEPs/OTEP-PREDICTIVE-TELEMETRY.md:\n- Comprehensive OpenTelemetry Enhancement Proposal drafted\n- Detailed architecture, use cases, implementation phases\n- Semantic conventions for predictive events\n- Performance benchmarks and privacy considerations\n- Ready for submission to OpenTelemetry Mobile SIG\n\n### .claude/ai_notes.md:\n- Updated project status to 70% complete \\(Phase 7 at 40%\\)\n- Documented recent achievements \\(Jan 22, 2026\\)\n- Added predictive telemetry to component structure\n- Updated next session priorities\n\n## Build Fixes\n\n- Created consumer-rules.pro \\(required by Android Gradle Plugin\\)\n- Fixed OTEL gauge type mismatches \\(ObservableDoubleMeasurement\\)\n- Resolved ConcurrentLinkedDeque.takeLast\\(\\) compatibility issues\n- All modules now compile cleanly\n\n## Testing Status\n\nBuild verification: ✅ SUCCESSFUL\n- otel-android-mobile library compiles without errors\n- Demo app assembles successfully\n- All 63 tasks complete \\(6 executed, 57 up-to-date\\)\n\nNext: Unit tests for predictive module \\(60 tests planned\\)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n\\)\")",
